<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>4.6.5: Interpreting Graphs</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00951</md:content-id>
    <md:title>4.6.5: Interpreting Graphs</md:title>
    <md:uuid>e866f0df-f6ac-4f0a-b8e5-6b0d06f10374</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section>
      <title>Cool Down Activity</title>
      <para>A squirrel runs up and down a tree.</para>
      <para>The graph shows the height of the squirrel, \(h\) (feet), as a function of time, \(t\) (seconds).</para>
      <para>
        <figure id="fig-00001">
          <media alt="Piecewise graph. Horizontal axis, 0 to 8, time, seconds. Vertical axis, 0 to 16, height, feet. Graph starts at 0 comma 9, increases, deceases to 4 comma 0, increases, then flattens out at 6 comma 10.">
            <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_04_09_12_01.svg"/>
          </media>
        </figure>
     </para>
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>What is the highest point the squirrel reaches?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para/>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para>14 feet</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>Solve \(h(t)=0\). What does this solution tell you about the squirrel?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para/>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para>\(t=4\) means that after 4 seconds, the squirrel is at the bottom of the tree on the ground.
   </para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>Find the vertical intercept of the graph. What does it tell you about the squirrel?</para>
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para/>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para>\((0,9)\) means that at the beginning, the squirrel is 9 feet high in the tree.
   </para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
    </section>
  </content>
</document>